2	-- Spaces readable by the caller are checked per row against LocalAccess, through its primary key, so single-account reads stay cheap.
3	-- Inside a policy, LocalAccess is filtered by its own reader-level select policy. Partial access goes through a definer view the planner can inline, and writes to LocalAccess itself go through account_ids_in_shared_spaces.
4	-- What the policies allow does not change.
